    "interpretation": "Robustness aligns with distance-to-benign, not with signature diversity. The two robust classes (fuzzing, max-speedometer) sit far from benign (~0.42-0.50); the two fragile classes (reverse-light-on/off) sit close (~0.04-0.09). All four classes fall in the predicted rank order. Descriptive corroboration only (n=4); rank agreement is stronger evidence than the coefficient. Limitation: global distance proxy, not a per-feature attack-path analysis.",
    "prediction_for_defence": "Adversarial training should help most where distance-to-benign is smallest (reverse-light classes) and little where it is largest (fuzzing, speedometer)."
  },
